# Story 70: Inspecting & Sending Across Panes (45s)
# Hook: Your agent can read another pane's state and even type into it -- with approval.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-070-inspecting-sending-across-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Your agent can read another pane's state and even type into it -- with approval.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and split a second pane so the agent has a neighbor to inspect and drive.

[00:09.0 --> 00:20.0]
From prompt mode, ask the agent who else is around. The agents_list tool shows every pane and its status.

[00:20.0 --> 00:32.0]
Ask it to inspect that other pane. pane_inspect reads the pane's recent output and state without you switching focus.

[00:32.0 --> 00:42.0]
Now have it send a command into that pane. pane_send injects input -- and because it acts elsewhere, it asks for approval.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Inspect, coordinate, and act across panes -- safely.

